\begin_layout Enumerate

\lang american
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset

-means clustering and PCA are both 
\emph on
unsupervised learning 
\emph default
methods and thus somehow try to extract patterns for understanding and or visualisation of the data.
 Typically in a data-exploratory state.
 One way they differ is in their concrete goal.
 The goal of PCA is to linearly reduce the dimensions needed to represent the information / variation in the data (or as much as possible).
 The goal of 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset

-means clustering is to identify datapoints 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in\mathbb{R}^{m}$
\end_inset

 that are share some similarities.
\end_layout

